ished off all of the  remaining upper moons but not without  heavy losses genya shinobu and muichiro  have all died and those who are alive  are looking far worse for wear slowly  the remaining demon slayers arrive to  the battlefield and muzon is demolishing  them even taking one of tonjiro's eyes  before poisoning him and leaving him  unconscious it isn't just tanjiru though  he is swatting off the other demon  slayers like they are less than flies  once all of the demon slayers have  assembled the group manages to push back  here and there but ultimately it comes  down to him being an immortal and having  infinite chances to strike back while  the demon slayers can barely afford to  be hit once without risking terrible  poisoning or worse and on top of this  they have to hold him off until sunrise  so things are looking pretty bleak  however tonjiro wakes up here and makes  his way back onto the battlefield having  just peered into ancestral memories and  learning the secrets of the 13th form of  sun breathing with this at his disposal  he can fight back but it takes all he  can do just to keep breathing while he  performs his attack muzon begins  recognizing that tanjiro is a threat but  says he's nothing compared to yorichi  but even so muzon is struggling for some  reason panicking he looks back into  tomio's memories to see what else the  drug might have done not only was the  drug meant to turn him human but it was  also causing him to age extremely fast  and over the course of the battle he had  already aged 9 000 years  which is why his hair hadn't returned to  being black he was slowing down and  that's why the slayers were starting to  get the upper hand we learn later that  the drug also prevents him from bursting  into thousands of fragments and escaping  that way as well and with all of those  parts in play the slayers can begin  their counter-attack scars begin  emerging all over muzon's body as it  can't keep up with its rapid  regeneration and they reveal where  yurichi cut him years and years ago this  shows the demon slayers where muzon's  vital organs were and marks the weak  points for them to attack with their red  blades  ultimately through a massive group  effort the odds fall in the demon  slayer's hands and they manage to corner  muzon as the sun rises in one final  gambit muzon creates a shell of flesh in  the form of a giant baby around his body  in hopes of protecting himself from the  sun long enough for him to escape but  it's no use the demon slayers manage to  hold him down and finally he is defeated  now it's a pretty direct parallel but i  know that a lot of people really don't  like the demon baby form so much so i'm  going to explain it anyways muzon was a  coward who relied on others for  protection he was nothing more than a  giant baby the entire series who would  put up walls and facades to hide himself  away while yes it does look admittedly  lame as hell  it's also incredibly fitting for a  monster who avoided cremation as a  stillborn to be burnt up in the sun as  he revealed himself to still be that  baby now that said muzon's story  technically doesn't end there the poison  he left within tonjiro actually had a  small bit of himself within it just  enough to cling on to the living cells  left within tonjiro's body and bring him  back to life as the inheritor of muzon's  will in the ultimate demon form but  while his will is being passed on this  isn't technically muzon himself  so if you want to learn more about that  form you'll have to check out our video  all about tanjiro's forms after this one  muzon really is an interesting demon  he's this cowardly mastermind pulling  the strings of others on his own quest  for immortality despite that he has this  overwhelming presence when he actually  shows up it kind of feels like you have  this superman-esque figure with next to  no weaknesses and incredible power  but even so he's still terrified at  every corner it's a pretty unique 